Here is the Java code to compute the factorial of a given number using a loop structure:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Factorial {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter a positive integer: ");
        int number = scanner.nextInt();

        long factorial = 1;

        for (int i = 1; i <= number; i++) {
            factorial *= i;
        }

        System.out.println("Factorial of " + number + " is: " + factorial);
    }
}
```

This code prompts the user to enter a positive integer, then uses a for loop to calculate the factorial of that number. The factorial is calculated by multiplying the current value of the factorial variable by the loop counter, starting from 1 and going up to the input number. Finally, the result is printed to the console.

